// An argument-count mismatch is fatal even where the call can never run.
//
// The check is static and a mismatch is never intentional, so the program is
// rejected rather than run up to the bad call. This is what the language has
// always done for a bare `f(a, b)`; the qualified form now matches it, and so
// does `run` — it used to reject the local form and execute this one.
<# ./lib_saludo => s

>> "vivo" ¶
? (#0) {
    s::saluda("ana", "sobra")
}
>> "fin" ¶
